From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Sep 2026 09:40:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] AMLCodec: let an AV1 temporal unit end after its last tile
 group

av1_parser_frame decides a frame is finished when the last tile group ends
exactly at the end of the packet, so a temporal unit that legally carries a
padding or metadata OBU after that tile group leaves seen_frame_header set.
The loop then reads an OBU header out of the zero bytes that remain and
returns -1, after it has already written every repacked byte.

That return was harmless while the caller ignored it. It is not harmless now
that the packet is dropped on a parse failure: a stream which pads its
temporal units loses every frame. Take the end of the input as the end of the
unit and keep the output that was produced. A truncated OBU still fails, in
the bounds checks that read it.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLCodec.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLCodec.cpp
@@ -1201,7 +1201,11 @@
         OBU_METADATA_TYPE meta_type;
         uint64_t type;
 
-        if (bytes_available == 0 && !seen_frame_header) {
+        // A temporal unit may legally end with padding or metadata after the
+        // last tile group, which leaves seen_frame_header set. The repacked
+        // output is already complete here: stop, rather than reading an OBU
+        // header out of the zero bytes that remain and calling it a failure.
+        if (bytes_available == 0) {
             break;
         }
 
